tions can be accessed, monitored, or compromised, how should people think about risk—and their own vulnerability?\nWe also explore questions of power and control operating beneath the surface. From blackmail and coercion to the role of information in maintaining influence, what mechanisms are at play—and how visible are they to the public?\nFinally, we discuss his latest book, Forbidden Facts, which examines contested ground in public health and institutional trust. Why are certain lines of inquiry discouraged or shut down entirely? And what happens when individuals begin to question the boundaries of what they’re told is acceptable to examine?\nThis is a conversation about intuition, power, and perception—and how to think clearly in a world where not everything is as it appears. Show less", "thumbnail": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/8f/s8/1/g/V/Y/n/gVYnA.qR4e-small-VSRF-Live-228-Government-Va..jpg", "display_id": "v77o9tq", "fulltitle": "VSRF Live #228 - Government Vaccine Deception", "duration_string": "1:35:36", "upload_date": "20260514", "release_date": "20260519", "release_year": 2026, "is_live": false, "was_live": true, "epoch": 1794321465, "acodec": "aac", "vcodec": "none", "url": "https://hugh.cdn.rumble.cloud/video/fww1/8f/s8/2/g/V/Y/n/gVYnA.Gaa.rec.aac", "format_id": "audio-192p", "tbr": 192, "filesize": 137681328, "width": 0, "height": 192, "protocol": "https", "ext": "aac", "audio_ext": "aac", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 192, "resolution": "audio only", "aspect_ratio": 0.0, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/148.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate"}, "format": "audio-192p - audio only", "_type": "video", "_version": {"version": "2026.11.04.232659", "release_git_head": "412e7f0a4b0588fe884a02b344ac66a06538475b", "repository"